{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.B3AggSecantCharacterisation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.B3AggSecantCharacterisation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Convex.Function"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.B3AggSecant.sign_carries_no_information_beyond_the_secant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.B3AggSecant.sign_carries_no_information_beyond_the_secant","kind":"theorem","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B3AggSecantCharacterisation.lean#L229-L237","doc":"**The fit statement, as a theorem rather than a caution.** For `g > 0` the\npredicate \"`Φ` has a non-negative 3-body cumulant at `g`\" is *logically\nequivalent* to a property of `Φ` alone — its origin-secant slope not falling\nacross `(g, 3g)`. The two are one proposition, so exhibiting an aggregator with\nthe second is not independent evidence for the first. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.B3AggSecant.b3Agg_pos_iff_exponent_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.B3AggSecant.b3Agg_pos_iff_exponent_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B3AggSecantCharacterisation.lean#L205-L225","doc":"**The power-law reading.** A `p`-homogeneous aggregator scales by `3 ^ p`, so\n`b₃ > 0` iff `p > 1`: the assembly must be *superlinear* in the bond count.\n`p = 1` is additive superposition and gives exactly zero; `p < 1` — which is\nwhere a concave law such as a logarithm sits — gives a negative cumulant.\n\nSo the open question \"why should the aggregator curve upward?\" becomes the\nsharper and more answerable \"**is the assembly law superlinear in the bond\ncount, and why?**\" That is a question about scaling, which the framework can in\nprinciple settle without reference to the measured sign. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.B3AggSecant.b3Agg_eq_zero_iff_scale_eq_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.B3AggSecant.b3Agg_eq_zero_iff_scale_eq_three","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B3AggSecantCharacterisation.lean#L193-L203","doc":"**`b₃` vanishes exactly at `c = 3`** — superposition, the affine boundary\nthat `b3Agg_linear_eq_zero` is the linear instance of. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.B3AggSecant.b3Agg_pos_iff_scale_gt_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.B3AggSecant.b3Agg_pos_iff_scale_gt_three","kind":"theorem","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B3AggSecantCharacterisation.lean#L182-L191","doc":"**The sign is then the scaling factor against 3, and nothing else.** For a\npositive aggregator value, `b₃ > 0` exactly when the law scales by more than the\nbond count it is scaling across. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.B3AggSecant.b3Agg_of_scales","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.B3AggSecant.b3Agg_of_scales","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B3AggSecantCharacterisation.lean#L175-L180","doc":"**The scaling identity.** If the aggregator scales by a factor `c` across the\nratio `3`, the cumulant is `(c − 3) Φ g` — no convexity, no differentiability,\nno hypothesis on `Φ` anywhere else. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.B3AggSecant.convexOn_sufficient_not_necessary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.B3AggSecant.convexOn_sufficient_not_necessary","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B3AggSecantCharacterisation.lean#L146-L152","doc":"**Convexity is sufficient and strictly unnecessary.** There is an aggregator\nthrough the origin that is *not* convex on `Ici 0` and still has a strictly\npositive 3-body cumulant — so a search for `b₃ > 0` restricted to convex\naggregators is searching a strict subset of what the cumulant admits. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.B3AggSecant.witnessPhi_not_convexOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.B3AggSecant.witnessPhi_not_convexOn","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B3AggSecantCharacterisation.lean#L134-L144","doc":"**It is not convex on `Ici 0`.** The midpoint of `[0, 1/3]` lies strictly\nabove the chord: `Φ (1/6) = −5/216` against a chord value of `−8/216`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.B3AggSecant.witnessPhi_b3Agg_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.B3AggSecant.witnessPhi_b3Agg_pos","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B3AggSecantCharacterisation.lean#L131-L132","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.B3AggSecant.witnessPhi_b3Agg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.B3AggSecant.witnessPhi_b3Agg","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B3AggSecantCharacterisation.lean#L127-L129","doc":"Its cumulant at `g = 1` is `18 > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.B3AggSecant.witnessPhi_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.B3AggSecant.witnessPhi_zero","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B3AggSecantCharacterisation.lean#L125-L125","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.B3AggSecant.witnessPhi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.B3AggSecant.witnessPhi","kind":"def","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B3AggSecantCharacterisation.lean#L120-L123","doc":"The witness aggregator `Φ x = x³ − x²`. It passes through the origin, is\n**concave near it** (`Φ'' x = 6x − 2 < 0` for `x < 1/3`), and yet has a strictly\npositive 3-body cumulant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.B3AggSecant.b3Agg_eq_zero_iff_secant_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.B3AggSecant.b3Agg_eq_zero_iff_secant_eq","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B3AggSecantCharacterisation.lean#L103-L116","doc":"**The cumulant vanishes exactly when the secant slope is unchanged.** The\naffine case `b3Agg_linear_eq_zero` is the instance where the slope is constant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.B3AggSecant.b3Agg_pos_iff_secant_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.B3AggSecant.b3Agg_pos_iff_secant_lt","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B3AggSecantCharacterisation.lean#L91-L101","doc":"**The characterisation, strict.** The same statement for a strictly positive\ncumulant — the sign the AME2020 comparison actually asks for. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.B3AggSecant.b3Agg_nonneg_iff_secant_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.B3AggSecant.b3Agg_nonneg_iff_secant_le","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B3AggSecantCharacterisation.lean#L78-L89","doc":"**The characterisation, non-strict.** For `g > 0`, `b₃ ≥ 0` exactly when the\norigin-secant slope does not fall from `g` to `3g`. An `iff` — this replaces the\ntwo one-way convexity implications with the condition they were approximating. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.B3AggSecant.b3Agg_eq_secant_gap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.B3AggSecant.b3Agg_eq_secant_gap","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B3AggSecantCharacterisation.lean#L72-L76","doc":"**The identity.** For `g ≠ 0` the cumulant is the secant gap, scaled by `3g`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.B3AggSecant.originSecant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.B3AggSecant.originSecant","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B3AggSecantCharacterisation.lean#L69-L70","doc":"The slope of the secant from the origin to `(x, Φ x)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.B3AggSecant.b3Agg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.B3AggSecant.b3Agg","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/B3AggSecantCharacterisation.lean#L65-L67","doc":"The connected 3-body cumulant, as in `AggregatorConvexityDichotomy`:\n`b₃ = B(3) − 3·B(2) = Φ (3g) − 3 Φ g`. Restated here so this file stands alone. ","signatureChunk":0}]}